# THE LOCAL FILES A NEW TASK FOLDER NEEDS, which git does not track and a fresh
# worktree therefore does not have. .gitignore pattern syntax; only files git
# already ignores are eligible, so nothing here can shadow the commit.
#
# Conductor and Claude Code read this same file for the same purpose, so this is
# one list and not a list per tool.
#
# NAMES, NOT CONTENTS. Committing this is committing the fact that a file is
# needed, which is the same thing .gitignore commits.

# Dependencies. Cloned, so on APFS the blocks are shared and this costs no disk.
/node_modules

# The app's own configuration. Without it loadConfig() falls back to defaults,
# which is a different app from the one in the checkout beside it: measured
# 2026-10-07, five of the seven task folders then live had no copy of this.
zero.config.json

# DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, so nobody adds them back wondering why:
#   cloud/team.config.json  belongs to the Mac, not the folder, and is read off
#                           the home directory (tests/the-team-key-belongs-to-
#                           the-mac-not-the-folder).
#   renderer/dist           build output. A copy of it is some OTHER commit's
#                           build, and `npm start` builds it anyway.
